  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming trade mission circular textiles</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ready-made garment (RMG) industry, a cornerstone of Bangladesh&apos;s economy, employs over 4 million people and contributes 10.35% to GDP. Despite its economic significance, the sector faces criticism due to its substantial environmental footprint, including significant waste generation and resource consumption. Embracing circular practices presents an opportunity to address these challenges by turning waste into a driver of economic growth and environmental responsibility. To reach a circular RMG-industry, Bangladesh needs access to new technologies, innovations and knowledge, which the Dutch private sector can offer. Organising a trade mission from Bangladesh to the Netherlands focussing on circularity in the textile industry will offer opportunities to strengthen the relationship between Bangladesh and the Netherlands and enhance private sector- and economic cooperation in the textile industry in the following sub-sectors: &#x2022;	Circular design; &#x2022;	Recycling of post-production waste;&#x2022;	Traceability;&#x2022;	Clean production (less use of chemicals, water and fossil energy and more use of green energy).Moreover, this trade mission will make Bangladeshi companies aware of opportunities and developments offered by Dutch businesses towards a circular textile sector.</narrative>
  </description>
